{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::source_node_id` identifies the criterion's\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The node this question is about.\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has one obligation. `Criterion::source_node_id` must identify the criterion's source node, which is the node the question is about.\n\n**Test.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` carries the `{test}` reference for the subject.\n\n**Test criterion.** The test criterion is `Review<O>/Criterion<Application>`. Its `source_node_id` returns the `source` field. `Review::new` sets that field to `domain.cache().intern_node(Node(1))`.\n\n**Assertions on the result of `verify`.** `validator.verify(descriptor())` produces a value. The test asserts `value.source_node_id() == intern_node(Node(1))`. This ties the node the validator reports to the node the criterion identified through `source_node_id`.\n\n**Assertions on the stored record.** After `store_evidence` and `load_evidence`, the test asserts `loaded.source_node_id() == value.source_node_id()`. The `load_evidence(&descriptor())` lookup finds the record only if the stored record is keyed by that same source node. A criterion with a different source node would therefore not match.\n\n**Residual risk.** The test uses a single source node, `Node(1)`. Sending every criterion to a fixed node other than the one returned would still fail the assertion, so this is adequate for a trait method that just names a node. The method has no conditional behaviour or distinct input classes beyond which node it returns.\n\nI found no unassessed obligation, marking gap or acknowledgment issue.",
